What each harness battery executes (inside one battery, all fresh processes):
  - 12 staged published-byte pin gates + double-reconstruction W equality gates,
  - 4 fresh re-executions of the published K1164 verifier
    (same-env x2, isolated cwd/HOME, isolated + PYTHONHASHSEED=random);
    each verifier invocation re-runs the published fold24 machine 4 times
    (including fold23 isolated rerun chains), the bundled independent auditor
    once, and the verifier's own 2 tamper cases; every invocation's audit JSON
    must equal the published audit byte-for-byte (c7e10332...),
  - stdout of all 4 verifier invocations byte-identical,
  - 3 harness-level tamper cases at publisher-untested offsets/surfaces:
      TA  W inputs/worklist.csv offset 404        XORED 0x01  -> rc 1, no audit, GATE FAILED
      TB  W fold23/output/win8-root208090020004-receipt-fold-20261120.json offset 3456 -> rc 1, no audit, GATE FAILED
      TC  pub receipt byte offset 2024 (verifier P-gate surface)                 -> rc 1, no audit, GATE FAILED
  Total fresh computation across the whole session: 13 verifier invocations
  (1 smoke + 3 batteries x 4) = 52 fresh fold24 machine executions with fold23
  chain reruns and 13 bundled-independent-auditor re-executions.

Earlier fail-closed interceptions (experimental facts, same defensive pattern as
K1158/K1160/K1164's pin-typo captures, all caught before any battery ran):
  (a) the first harness build carried a W manifest digest constant computed with
      a different path scheme (leading "./" from a shell-side manifest); the
      harness's own W-tree-digest pin gate failed the run before any verifier
      execution; the constant was re-derived from the harness-canonical scheme.
  (b) the second build's staging feed loop attempted to pin bytes that are not
      fed to the verifier (experiment README/build_fold24.py): FileNotFoundError,
      fixed to gate exactly the six fed files. The published harness is the fixed
      one; both failures are recorded here, not hidden.

